<!-- The Android 12+ starting-window icon: the launch splash's first frame, drawn by the system.
     Same silhouette, size and position as AppLaunchSplash's empty vessel, so the handover from
     the system splash to the Compose one is invisible and the liquid simply starts pouring.
     288dp is the platform's canvas for an icon with no background; only its central 192dp circle
     is shown, and this mark's farthest point sits 90dp from centre. Neutral white rather than
     the accent: this cannot know the viewer's theme, so the empty glass is colourless on both
     sides of the handover and only the liquid takes the accent.
     Fork: the te mark (Yuji Syuku), traced like the loader's own silhouette; the OG's
     a-with-play-triangle went with the OG's logo and its video intro. -->
